{{Quote|Rex, what do we know about this place?''"<br />"''On this part of Skako, there's a race of locals, the Poletecs. All we know is they're very primitive.''"<br />"''Primitive is being kind. My intel says the Poletecs worship flying reptiles.|Anakin Skywalker receives intel from Rex and Tech|<ref name="A Distant Echo" />}}
The '''Poletecs''' were a [[species]] of [[Color|purple]], red, or beige-skinned, lanky [[humanoid]]s [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Skako Minor]]. During the [[Clone Wars]], [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]], and [[Clone Force 99]] encountered the inhabitants of a [[Poletec village]] while on a [[Mission to Skako Minor (Clone Wars)|mission]] to rescue their fellow [[clone trooper]] [[Echo]]. Later, the [[Galactic Republic]] [[trooper]]s were forced to visit the village a second time to ask for aid from the Poletec leader, [[Qin Yazal]]. The [[chief]]tain was reluctant at first, however he was eventually convinced. Both [[Cloning|clones]] and Poletecs fought advancing [[droid]]s from the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] [[Separatist Droid Army|army]]. With help from Skywalker, the [[Standard day|day]] was won for the [[The galaxy|Galactic]] Republic, and the Poletec chieftain told the [[Jedi]] that the Republic would always have an ally on Skako Minor.

==Biology and appearance==
The Poletecs were a [[species]] of [[Color|purple]], red, or beige-skinned, lanky [[humanoid]]s [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Skako Minor]]. They seemed to lack any form of hair, and their jaws were shaped sharply. They had elongated fingers, and protruding spikes, similar to [[eye]]brows.

Many Poletecs carried on one [[Limb|forearm]] primitive crustacean-like [[Poletec weapon|weaponry]] which fired black balls when swung. The red-skinned Poletecs seemed to be in greater numbers than the beige, and the purple seemed to be exclusive to the few Poletecs who rode on [[keeradak]]s.<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks">{{TCW|On the Wings of Keeradaks}}</ref>

==Society and culture==
[[File:Poletec-Chief-Discussion.png|thumb|left|220px|The Poletec leader consulted with his tribesmen.]]
The Poletecs were a primitive people who inhabited villages. They were said to worship the winged [[reptile]]s known as [[keeradak]]s, which they used as mounted steeds for [[transport]].<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" /> By [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates both the [[Trial of Ahsoka Tano]] and the [[Operation: Knightfall|siege of the Jedi Temple]] to [[19 BBY]]. Because the events of [[The Bad Batch (episode)|The Bad Batch]] take place after [[Ahsoka Tano]]'s trial, and before the Siege of the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]], it can be concluded that "The Bad Batch"'s events also occurred in 19 BBY.</ref> they had developed a [[Poletec language|native language]], speaking only in their native [[Language|tongue]]. By the [[time]] of the [[Clone Wars]], Poletecs still led a primitive lifestyle, with several using [[spear]]s as weapons, and were wary of offworlders. The Poletecs did not want to get involved in the Clone Wars initially, regarding it as an outsiders' conflict. The [[Skakoan]] [[foreman]] of the [[Techno Union]], [[Wat Tambor]], regarded the Poletecs as inferior beings.<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />

==History==
{{Quote|He said the Jedi will always have an ally here on Skako Minor.|Qin Yazal, as [[Language|translated]] by [[Tech]]|<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />}}
[[File:Poletec-Lying-In-Wait.png|thumb|right|220x220px|The Poletecs varied greatly in the color of their skin.]]
The [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]], and [[Clone Force 99]] encountered the inhabitants of a [[Poletec village]] while on a [[Mission to Skako Minor (Clone Wars)|mission]] to rescue the [[clone trooper]] [[Echo]]<ref name="A Distant Echo" /> in 19 BBY.<ref name="Date" /> Skywalker had been captured by the Poletecs, and when the [[Cloning|clone]] [[trooper]]s attempted to rescue Skywalker, a brief skirmish broke out. However, with the trooper [[Tech]] serving as a translator, Skywalker managed to convince the Poletec leader,<ref name="A Distant Echo" /> [[Qin Yazal]],<ref name="Character Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: Character Encyclopedia - Join the Battle!]]''</ref> that they did not pose a threat and that their true enemy was the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatists]]. While the Poletecs did not want to get involved in the Clone Wars, they provided the [[Galactic Republic]] [[Republic Military|forces]] with two [[scout]]s.<ref name="A Distant Echo" />

The scouts agreed to accompany the offworlders to the [[city]] [[Purkoll]] but no further.<ref name="A Distant Echo" /> Skywalker and the clones managed to escape back to the Poletec village on the wings of keeradaks, earning the respect of the Poletec villagers. Skywalker and the clones then convinced the Poletecs to help them fight against the Techno Union's [[droid]] [[Confederacy military|forces]].<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />

[[File:Poletec-Warriors-Battle.png|thumb|left|220x220px|The Poletecs during the battle.]]
Rolling a large stone down a slope, the Poletecs were able to create a distraction to ambush the Separatist forces, beginning the battle. Despite their initial success, many Poletec warriors were killed by the highly advanced [[Octuptarra tri-droid]]s and [[D1-series aerial battle droid]]s during the fighting. By the battle's end, the Poletec [[chief]]'s life had been saved several times by the Republic forces. Eventually, the battle was won by Clone Force 99 and all surviving Poletecs, with the help of Skywalker, and the survivors cheered in triumph in their native tongue. The Poletec chief later thanked the Republic for their help, and said that they would always have an ally on Skako Minor.<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:PoletecChiefConceptArt.jpg|thumb|right|220x220px|Concept art for the Poletec chieftain by [[Darren Marshall]].]]
{{Quote|The Techno Union owns everything on this planet, including the primitives.|Wat Tambor, in the story reel for "On the Wings of Keeradaks"|<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />}}
Poletecs first appeared in the [[canon]] but unfinished story reel episode of [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''The Clone Wars'' series]], "[[A Distant Echo]]." The episode premiered on [[April 17]], [[2015]], and was released on the [[StarWars.com|official ''Star Wars'' website]] soon after, as part of [[The Clone Wars Legacy|''The Clone Wars'' Legacy]].<ref name="Bad Batch panel">{{SWYouTube|HrulKkPjFms|Bad Batch Star Wars: The Clone Wars Panel &#124; Star Wars Celebration Anaheim|sw_url=video/bad-batch-star-wars-the-clone-wars-panel-star-wars-celebration-anaheim}}</ref> On [[February 28]], [[2020]], the final version of this episode was released on [[Disney+]].<ref name="Press Release">{{WebCite|url=https://collider.com/new-on-disney-plus-february-2020|text=What's New on Disney Plus February 2020, Including Toy Story 4|author=Gregory Lawrance|archivedate=20200125032840}}</ref>

[[Dee Bradley Baker]], the voice of all clone troopers in the ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' animated series, improvised the [[Poletec language|Poletec]] [[language]] and used the backwards speech from the red room in the series [[Wikipedia:Twin Peaks|''Twin Peaks'']] as inspiration.<ref name="Bad Batch panel" />

The episode "[[On the Wings of Keeradaks]]" was first released in [[2015]] as an unfinished story reel before the completed version premiered on [[Disney+]] in [[2020]]. In the story reel version, [[Wat Tambor]] demonstrated a deadly device, the [[S/D Decimator droid|organic decimator]], on a defenseless [[Unidentified Poletec test subject|Poletec test subject]] in an attempt to intimidate [[Anakin Skywalker]] into surrendering. However, the scene was not included in the final version of the episode.<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />

